@@ -55,10 +55,14 @@ the current state. `SessionEnd` records an attributed
 run, pick a run by project name, or forward the host's raw payload.
 
 SessionStart keeps its one-second socket inactivity limit. SessionEnd allows one
-request up to three seconds of socket inactivity, so a durable acknowledgement
-slower than one second can be confirmed without another request. Both hosts bound
-the SessionEnd command process to five seconds. The socket limit alone is not a
-wall-time deadline. A timeout remains unobserved; it never becomes task success.
+request up to two seconds of socket inactivity, so a durable acknowledgement
+slower than one second can still be confirmed without another request, while the
+whole end process, interpreter start and local state included, stays inside the
+host wall-time cap. Installed Codex clamps a SessionEnd hook command to three
+seconds of wall time, so the Codex hook files declare three rather than five;
+Claude Code keeps its five-second budget. The socket limit is inactivity, not a
+wall-time deadline, which is why it leaves headroom under that cap. A timeout
+remains unobserved; it never becomes task success.
 
